details.contract:
Add above `Coverage` in src/shared/envelope.ts:
```ts
export interface TestCensusEntry {
  language: string;
  nodes: number;
}

/** The test corpus this graph indexed. `nodes: 0` with `languages: []` is "no test symbols
 * were indexed", which is a different fact from "nothing covers this change". */
export interface TestCensus {
  nodes: number;
  languages: TestCensusEntry[];
}
```
`Coverage` gains exactly one member, after `not_indexed`:
```ts
  /** Indexed test symbols and the languages they come from (TOOLS-SPEC.md §1.1). Optional: only
   * the tools that render it pay the query. */
  tests?: TestCensus;
```
`ReadStatus` gains one member, after `stale_checked_at`:
```ts
  /** `!stale`, filled by the composition root after the handler answered (src/index.ts,
   * `route()` and `uncheckedReadStatus()`). Optional here because no handler sets it and a
   * hand-written ReadStatus fake predating the field must still type-check. */
  decisive?: boolean;
```
Do not add a tenth top-level envelope field, do not make either member required, and do not touch `Totals` (the repo-wide count is `not_indexed_total`, which the `${string}_total` index signature already admits).

Prepared statements only, through `prepared(conn, "<stable key>", build)`, one per query; never build a query in a loop. Exact SQL:
- `notIndexedAll` (key `coverage.notIndexedAll`): `SELECT ni.id, ni.path, ni.reason, ni.detail, ni.language FROM not_indexed ni ORDER BY ni.path, ni.reason` — same row shape as the existing `coverage.notIndexed/*` statement in `src/shared/store/read/coverage.ts`.
- `notIndexedCount` (key `coverage.notIndexedCount`): `SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM not_indexed`.
- `testsCensus` (key `files.testsCensus`): `SELECT f.language AS language, COUNT(*) AS nodes FROM node n JOIN file f ON f.id = n.file_id WHERE n.is_test = 1 GROUP BY f.language ORDER BY nodes DESC, f.language ASC`.
Signatures to add on `GraphReader` (src/shared/store/read/reader.ts), wired beside `rowsForPaths`/`censusByLanguage` in `makeReader`:
```ts
  /** Every skipped path in the graph, not just those under a requested prefix. */
  notIndexedAll(): readonly SkippedPathRow[];
  /** The repo-wide number of skipped paths: the one total every tool can agree on. */
  notIndexedCount(): number;
  /** Indexed test symbols and the languages behind them. */
  testsCensus(): TestCensus;
```
`testsCensus` returns `{ nodes: sum, languages: [{language, nodes}] }` where a null `file.language` is rendered as the string `"unknown"` (the same way `censusByLanguage` handles it — check and follow that code). Keep `src/shared/store/read/coverage.ts` free of `TestCensus` (that type lives in `#shared/envelope`). Do not change `rowsForPaths`, `censusByLanguage`, or any existing cache key.

```ts
export interface CoverageSource {
  readonly rowsForPaths: (paths: readonly string[]) => PathCoverage;
  readonly unresolvedForFiles: (fileIds: readonly number[]) => readonly UnresolvedRef[];
  /** The repo-wide skipped-path count (`reader.notIndexedCount()`). */
  readonly notIndexedCount: () => number;
}

export interface CoverageAssembly {
  readonly coverage: Coverage;
  readonly unresolved: readonly UnresolvedRef[];
  readonly relation: TotalRelation;
  /** `coverage.skipped` is scoped to `scope.paths`; this is the whole graph. Never smaller than
   * `coverage.not_indexed.length`. */
  readonly notIndexedTotal: number;
}
```
`coverage.skipped` stays `skipped.length` (the scoped count) — do not make it repo-wide; `coverageSource(conn)` gains the `notIndexedCount` projection. Update the module doc comment to say why two numbers exist, in one or two lines.
